ST  - Citizen Earthquake Science in Taiwan
UR  - https://www.fujipress.jp/jdr/dr/dsstr001200061174
Y2  - 2022/11/20/
L1  - https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/c7f1/9f6cc6e81c0dd63200b8157602cc2efe6981.pdf
N1  - <div data-schema-version="9"><p>BOINC criterion evidence - Survey report, verbatim: "Second, by collaborating with Stanford University to maintain a regional Quake-Catcher Network (QCN) server in Taiwan, we have promoted citizen seismology in Asia by bringing earthquake information and scientific knowledge to the public. More than 200 school teachers have already installed the QCN sensors in Internet-enabled computers." | PARTIAL EVIDENCE / INDIRECT CHAIN: this paper has no BOINC mention, but its subject is the QCN server and QCN sensors. QCN sensors run on BOINC clients - see the verbatim project-description passages in the 2009 IEEE record (DOI 10.1109/MIM.2009.5338255) and the 2009 SRL record (DOI 10.1785/gssrl.80.1.26) in this same RIS file. | Full text: J-STAGE / Journal of Disaster Research open-access PDF | Verification: full text checked 2026-11-10.</p>
</div>
